ealth and food. Modeling nutritional and dietary transitions with regard to obesity and associated pathologies, agro-food alternatives, nutritional and environmental health, 1000 days, One Health.\r\nFood: food socialization; social issues relating to food, knowledge and practices in the medical field concerning obesity, cancer, aging, disability, etc.; medicalization of food, scientific and socio-technical controversies, consumer communication strategies; relations between health and food, competition and conflicts between social and medical standards; food risks and concerns, collective/communicative risk management mechanisms, public food policies and links with food heritages; empirical ethics, experimental empirical mechanisms.\r\nHealth: reconfigurations of healthcare systems, combined developments towards ambulatory care, telemedicine, empowerment and therapeutic patient education, transformations of healthcare work and associated new issues in terms of patients' rights and medical responsibility; recompositions of medical and nursing work, computerized applications; global political injunctions and intersectional inequalities in health, political space of health, political construction of the relationship to health, production of healthcare norms, and their application or contestation by users and civil society.\r\nResearch areas: Metropolitan France, Overseas France (Guadeloupe, Martinique, French Guiana, Mayotte, Reunion Island, New Caledonia, French Polynesia), Andorra, Poland, Southeast Asia (Malaysia, Indonesia, Vietnam, Singapore), Bali, Japan, Brazil.	#https://certop.cnrs.fr/presentation-axe-sante-et-alimentation-santal/#	#https://certop.cnrs.fr/santal-axis-health-and-food/#	\N	\N
3	1	TERNOV	Transitions écologiques. Risques, Innovations, Tourisme	Ecological transitions. Risks, Innovations, Tourism	Saliha HADNA-BREMAND; Nicolas PILUSO	Transition écologique et activités socio-économiques.\r\nDispositifs d’action publique territorialisés (ressource en eau, autonomie énergétique, déchets,… ), tensions entre usages (agriculture et eau potable…), tensions entre modèles technico-économiques (gestion centralisée ou décentralisée de l’énergie… ), mise en justice des problèmes d’environnement.\r\nPolitisation de la production, marchandisation de la nature, mise en cause de la recherche scientifique (rapports entre sphère de la recherche et société civile, place de la recherche dans la gestion et le contrôle des risques émergents), réglementation et effets sur les risques.\r\nTransition énergétique : nouveau contrat avec l’environnement entre pouvoirs publics, acteurs économiques et société civile, justice environnementale, nouvelles formes de gouvernance et d’organisation multi-acteurs, inégalités sociales, outils d’accompagnement au changement (secteurs du bâtiment, des déchets et des transports).\r\nTransition touristique, tensions territoriales entre tourisme et problématiques environnementales, patrimonialisation dans ses recompositions socioculturelles et économiques, tourisme dans de grandes destinations phares (Egypte, Tunisie, Maroc, Syrie, Mésopotamie).	Ecological transition and socio-economic activities.\r\nTerritorialized public action mechanisms (water resources, energy autonomy, waste, etc.), tensions between uses (agriculture and drinking water, …), tensions between technical-economic models (centralized or decentralized energy management, ...), bringing environmental problems to justice.\r\nPoliticization of production, commodification of nature, questioning of scientific research (relations between the research sphere and civil society, the role of research in the management and control of emerging risks), regulation and effects on risks.\r\nEnergy transition: a new contract with the environment between public authorities, economic players and civil society, environmental justice, new forms of governance and multi-actor organization, social inequalities, tools to support change (building, waste and transport sectors).\r\nTourism transition, territorial tensions between tourism and environmental issues, heritage in its socio-cultural and economic recompositions, tourism in major flagship destinations (Egypt, Tunisia, Morocco, Syria, Mesopotamia).	#https://certop.cnrs.fr/presentation-axe-ternov/#	#https://certop.cnrs.fr/ternov-axis-ecological-transitions-risks-innovations-tourism/#	\N	\N
