regnancy and different stages of child development. Impact of medical practices, pre-natal, peri-natal, and postnatal interventions on mothers’ health, and the psychomotor, cognitive, social and emotional development of children and adolescents, including long-term comorbidities. Contexts of vulnerability. Implementation and monitoring of interventions. Public health strategies orientation (prevention and care recommendations).\r\nMaternal and foetal health: foetal heart rate monitoring, labour, pre-eclampsia, twin pregnancies, premature delivery. Medicine exposure during pregnancy and breastfeeding:  teratogenic and foetotoxic risks, long-term effects; risk profiles. Child disability: early screening in vulnerable populations, epidemiology of neurodevelopmental disabilities, individual, family and societal impact of disability. Mental health risk from babies to adolescents: developmental trajectories and vulnerability factors / frailties (psycho-trauma, vulnerable parenting, psychotropic drugs). Global perinatal, child and adolescent health in Africa: strategies for the prevention and management of chronic infectious diseases in children (HIV-Aids, Hepatitis B virus, SARS-Cov2-Covid, pneumonia), evaluation of prevention programmes for adolescent global health. Oral diseases / periodontitis: determinants and risk factors in certain vulnerable populations, risk of systemic diseases with an inflammatory component (obstetric pathologies, adverse pregnancy outcomes, severe mental disorders such as major depression or autism spectrum disorders), oral and periodontal microbiota.	#https://cerpop.inserm.fr/equipe-sphere#	#https://cerpop.inserm.fr/cerpop-equipe-sphere-eng#	\N	\N
