unity and environment / Influence of microbial or fungal AM signals on root development and plant nutritional status / Plant and or bacterial actors controlling host specificity and partner choice in RL symbiosis / How root barrier deposition is coordinated with the establishment of endosymbiosis (role of the endodermis).\r\nActive oxygen species (AOS) / Rhizobial and mycorrhizal lipo-chitooligosaccharide (LCO) signals; mechanisms of rhizobial LCO perception (Nod, NF factors) and how they control nodulation and root infection in legumes; interactions with auxin signaling and homeostasis. / Genes encoding Medicago truncatula Lysin-motif receptor-like kinases (MtNFP and MtLYK9). \r\nModel plants: truncated alfalfa (Medicago truncatula) and pea (Pisum sativum).\r\nApproaches: genetics, association genetics, biochemistry, cell biology, transcriptomics, imaging.	https://www.lipme.fr/sms	https://www.lipme.fr/en/sms	\N	\N
